## 3. Function Call Chain & Reachability

### Call Graph:
```
ixheaace_testbench.c (main entry point)
    ↓
ixheaace_read_drc_config_params() [impd_drc_user_config.c:74]
    ├→ impd_drc_get_integer_value() [impd_drc_user_config.c:56] (multiple calls)
    │   └→ Buffer over-read vulnerability
    └→ impd_drc_get_float_value() [impd_drc_user_config.c:40] (multiple calls)
        └→ Buffer over-read vulnerability
```

### Entry Point Evidence:
In `ixheaace_testbench.c`, the function is declared:
```c
#include "impd_drc_user_config.h"
```

The testbench reads a DRC configuration file (`DRC_CONFIG_FILE "impd_drc_config_params.txt"` at line 95) and would call `ixheaace_read_drc_config_params()` to parse it.

